{%- comment -%}
  Contact page.

  Same reasoning as the FAQ page: the nav points at the homepage anchor, but
  /pages/contact-us is indexed and its handle is fixed by Decision #9, so the
  page stays and simply renders the designed section instead of the stock Dawn
  form it used to.

  Assign this template to the Contact Us page in Shopify admin:
    Content -> Pages -> Contact Us -> Theme template -> "contact-us"

  Note this replaces templates/page.contact.json, Dawn's unstyled contact
  template — which is exactly the "blank or off-design page" problem that
  prompted keeping these pages properly rather than deleting them.

  The hidden <h1> is the page's own title, so the document has one first-level
  heading above the section's <h2>. See page.faqs.liquid for the full reasoning.
{%- endcomment -%}

<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>

{% section 'ness-contact' %}
